{"version":2,"id":"new-york-harbor","title":"New York Harbor","titleLines":["New York","Harbor"],"subtitle":"A Week of Currents","region":"Mid-Atlantic","blurb":"The tide reaches New York Harbor through the Narrows and then splits: up the Hudson, through the East River and Hell Gate to Long Island Sound, and around Staten Island through the Kills. The East River is a tidal strait, not a river, and it reverses four times a day. The fastest surface current in this week of the model was 4.0 knots. The model has no water temperature, so the color is the temperature at the NOAA gauge at the Battery, the same over the whole harbor.","model":"NYOFS","modelLong":"NOAA New York and New Jersey Harbor Operational Forecast System","agency":"NOAA","tzLabel":"EDT","utcOffsetHours":-4,"startLocal":"2026-09-21T00:00","hours":169,"width":748,"height":697,"maskWidth":1496,"maskHeight":1394,"bbox":{"lon0":-74.53953,"lon1":-73.53047,"lat0":40.30849,"lat1":41.02151},"core":{"x0":0.26711,"x1":0.73289,"y0":0.19847,"y1":0.80153},"metersPerPixel":113.751,"tempC":{"min":20.9,"max":21.0},"legendF":{"min":66,"max":76},"velModes":12,"tempModes":4,"meanVelScale":0.280677,"velCoef":[[-0.376745,0.320203,-0.068648,0.083055,0.05695,-0.023188,0.092602,-0.076783,0.031455,-0.012048,0.040052,-0.020682],[0.314666,0.367298,-0.098975,0.062352,0.091768,-0.014533,0.065133,-0.013061,0.030044,-0.028809,0.066427,-0.019249],[0.935734,0.173919,0.030814,-0.152278,0.085742,-0.061713,0.043996,0.017401,0.01665,0.006362,0.067434,-0.011219],[1.151575,-0.033058,0.085877,-0.12165,0.041124,-0.049774,-0.005045,-0.026992,0.023146,0.034201,0.052247,0.009],[1.020518,-0.224243,0.097045,0.017844,0.023143,-0.034469,0.039327,-0.031575,0.037559,0.014223,0.042264,0.025097],[0.658385,-0.355057,0.055166,0.166695,0.038344,-0.028948,0.093602,-0.003099,0.053039,-0.014798,0.029791,0.015185],[0.152473,-0.377415,-0.033279,0.234181,0.048485,-0.054012,0.045407,-0.007646,0.047719,0.005301,0.017931,-0.020574],[-0.424059,-0.274549,-0.177712,0.0